# Requests to try with VS Code's REST Client extension.
# On your computer: start the API first (npm run dev), then click Send Request above any request.
# Online: put your Render address in place of http://localhost:3100 on the next line, such as
# https://your-service-name.onrender.com, and send the same requests to the live API.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3100

### Is it working? 200 with { "status": "ok" }
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Every trail, sorted by name: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/trails

### Only the muddy trails (Lookout Ridge Trail and Meadow View Loop): 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/trails?status=muddy

### A status that isn't open, muddy or closed: 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/trails?status=icy

### One trail by its slug: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/trails/bear-hollow

### A trail that doesn't exist: 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/trails/moon-trail
